k"},{"name":"TestBouncer_SeedCall_HappyPath","reason":"pins the seed call's spec, pointer and focus file, and that it writes no verdict or ledger"},{"name":"TestBouncer_SeedDiscriminator_ParsesRatherThanStats","reason":"pins that a present but unparseable focus file is archived and re-seeded rather than treated as a re-bounce"},{"name":"TestBouncer_SeedSideHarvest_SurvivesALateFailure","reason":"pins that a focus file the seed agent wrote survives a late run error or a non-Done outcome byte-identical"},{"name":"TestBouncer_Verdict_CirclingReturnsAwaitingAndReplaysWithoutSpawning","reason":"pins that a CIRCLING verdict returns Awaiting naming the round and cause, and that a fresh Bouncer over the same run dir replays it without spawning"},{"name":"TestBouncer_Verdict_CirclingWithLiveJudgeAttachesAndHarvests","reason":"pins that a CIRCLING verdict with a live judge attaches to it, never respawns, and keeps the judge's own next-round focus file"},{"name":"TestBouncer_Verdict_LegacyWordAtEntry","reason":"pins how a legacy verdict word on disk at Call entry is read: APPROVED clears and re-seeds, BLOCKING replays as a Stuck over the ledger"},{"name":"TestComputeRoundFacts_GatingRule","reason":"pins the gating rule of the round facts: MEDIUM design findings are gating, a BLOCKING scope finding is counted but not gating"},{"name":"TestDecisionRuleMarker_CirclingOnlyFromTheCheckpoint","reason":"pins the decision rule's text: both non-circling verdicts are always offered, the rising-count caveat comes with CIRCLING, and round 2 on renders the lighter rule with its earlier-open list and round-1 fallback"},{"name":"TestEntryErrAndCancelErr","reason":"pins that the entry and cancel errors name the producer and engine, wrap the context error and read differently"},{"name":"TestEscalation_AbsentRecord","reason":"pins that an absent escalation record reads as absent with no error"},{"name":"TestEscalation_RoundTrip","reason":"pins the escalation record's round trip: cause, notice, 